You are implementing bead vamsa-ywo.7: GEDCOM Data Mapper (GEDCOM ↔ Vamsa) for the vamsa family tree application.

## Context
- The GEDCOM parser (vamsa-ywo.6) is complete and working
- You have access to ParsedIndividual, ParsedFamily types from parser
- Target: Bidirectional mapping between GEDCOM and Vamsa data models
- Focus: Preserve all data through import and export cycles

## Task: Create Data Mapper

### 1. Analyze Vamsa Data Models

First, examine the existing Vamsa models in the codebase:

```bash
grep -r "model Person" src/
grep -r "model Relationship" src/
grep -r "enum RelationType" src/
```

Understand:
- Person fields (id, firstName, lastName, gender, dateOfBirth, dateOfPassing, birthPlace, profession, bio, etc.)
- Relationship types (SPOUSE, PARENT, CHILD, etc.)
- How gender is stored (enum values)
- Date storage format

### 2. Create Mapper Types (`src/lib/gedcom/mapper-types.ts`)

```typescript
